From: knulli <knulli@knulli>
Subject: [PATCH] SystemScreenSaver: close the slideshow branch

The "slideshow" branch of startScreenSaver() opens a block that is never
closed: the "}" at the end of the "if (!path.empty())" body is followed
directly by "else if (screensaver_behavior == \"power save\")", so that
else-if chains onto the inner path test instead of the outer behaviour
chain, and the function body is left one brace short.

Everything after it is then parsed as if still inside startScreenSaver(),
which is why the errors land in unrelated headers:

  SystemScreenSaver.cpp:238:40: error: qualified-id in declaration before
  ComponentList.h:10:1: error: 'namespace' definition is not allowed here
  GuiFileBrowser.h:7:1: error: a template declaration cannot appear at block scope

Signed-off-by: knulli <knulli@knulli>
---
diff --git a/es-app/src/SystemScreenSaver.cpp b/es-app/src/SystemScreenSaver.cpp
--- a/es-app/src/SystemScreenSaver.cpp
+++ b/es-app/src/SystemScreenSaver.cpp
@@ -224,6 +224,7 @@
 			mTimer = 0;
 			return;
 		}
+	}
 	else if (screensaver_behavior == "power save")
 	{
 		mPowerSave = true;
